show_reminder() {
cat <<'REMINDER'
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
📌 crecall Quick Reminder

💡 Memory is your flagship feature - never lose context again!
   Use: crecall --memory add "important note here"

⚙️  Settings can be changed via: crecall --settings (coming soon)
📖 Full help: crecall --help
🔧 API docs: http://localhost:8000/docs (if backend running)

🎯 Quick commands:
   -s, --save          Save checkpoint
   -m, --memory        Memory commands (add/list/clear)
   -S, --summary       Show session summary
   -v, --version       Show version
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
REMINDER
}

main() {
  init_dirs
  
  # Check for crash recovery on first run (unless it's help/version)
  local raw="${1:-}"
  if [ -z "$raw" ]; then
    # Check for crash and offer recovery
    if [ -f "$DATA_HOME/crash_marker.json" ]; then
      echo "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
      echo "⚠️  Crash detected from previous session!"
      echo "━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
      echo ""
      echo "Run 'crecall-recover' to restore your work."
      echo ""
    fi
    show_reminder
    exit 0
  fi
  # Require leading dash for any command
  case "$raw" in
    --*|-*) ;; 
    *) echo 'Invalid command. Use "crecall --help" for more information.'; exit 1;;
  esac
  # Map short flags to long command tokens
  local cmd="$raw"
  case "$cmd" in
    -s|--save) cmd="save";;
    -S|--summary|--refer) cmd="summary";;
    -t|--total) cmd="total";;
    -T|--total-encrypt) cmd="total-encrypt";;
    -r|--resume) cmd="resume";;
    -p|--pause) cmd="pause";;
    -m|--memory) cmd="memory";;
    -c|--clip) cmd="clip";;
    --clipped|clipped) cmd="clipped";;
    sync) cmd="sync";;
    -e|--encrypt) cmd="encrypt";;
    -d|--decrypt) cmd="decrypt";;
    --cache) cmd="cache";;
    -D|--data) cmd="data";;
    -x|--state) cmd="state";;
    -v|--version) cmd="version";;
    -h|--help|--usage) cmd="help";;
    -o|--settings) cmd="settings";;
    *) echo 'Invalid command. Use "crecall --help" for more information.'; exit 1;;
  esac
  shift || true
  case "$cmd" in
    save) save_checkpoint "$@" ;;
    summary) summary ;;
    total) transcript_plain "$@" ;;
    total-encrypt) transcript_encrypt "$@" ;;
    resume) resume "$@" ;;
    pause) manual_pause ;;
    memory)
      local sub="${1:-}"
      shift || true
      case "$sub" in
        add) memory_add "$@" ;;
        list) memory_list "$@" ;;
        clear) memory_clear ;;
        resume|load) memory_resume "$@" ;;
        search) memory_search "$@" ;;
        *) echo 'Invalid memory subcommand. Use: memory add|list|clear|resume|search'; exit 1;;
      esac ;;
    clip|clipped)
          sync)
            local sub="${1:-}"; shift || true
            case "$sub" in
              push)
                local host="${1:-}"; test -n "$host" || { echo 'Host required: crecall sync push <host>'; exit 1; }
                echo '[crecall] Pushing bundle to remote...'
                curl -s -X POST "$API_URL/portable/push-remote?host=$host" | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null || true
                ;;
              pull)
                local host="${1:-}"; test -n "$host" || { echo 'Host required: crecall sync pull <host>'; exit 1; }
                echo '[crecall] Pulling bundle from remote...'
                curl -s -X POST "$API_URL/portable/pull-remote?host=$host" | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null || true
                ;;
              *) echo 'Invalid sync subcommand. Use: sync push|pull <host>'; exit 1;;
            esac
            ;;
      local sub="${1:-}"
      shift || true
      case "$sub" in
        add) clip_add "$@" ;;
        list|ls) clip_list "$@" ;;
        resume|restore|load) clip_resume "$@" ;;
        clear|prune) clip_clear ;;
        *) echo 'Invalid clip subcommand. Use: clip add|list|resume|clear'; exit 1;;
      esac ;;
    encrypt) encrypt_file "$@" ;;
    decrypt) decrypt_file "$@" ;;
    cache)
      test "${1:-}" = 'prune' || { echo 'Invalid cache subcommand. Use: cache prune'; exit 1; }
      shift || true
      cache_prune "$@" ;;
    data)
      test "${1:-}" = 'clear' || { echo 'Invalid data subcommand. Use: data clear'; exit 1; }
      data_clear ;;
    state) cat "$STATE_FILE" 2>/dev/null || echo '{}' ;;
    version) echo "$VERSION" ;;
    help) show_help ;;
    settings) settings_menu ;;
    *) echo 'Invalid command. Use "crecall --help" for more information.'; exit 1 ;;
  esac
}

CONFIG_FILE="$DATA_HOME/config.json"

load_config() {
  if [ -f "$CONFIG_FILE" ]; then
    CONFIG_JSON=$(cat "$CONFIG_FILE")
  else
    CONFIG_JSON='{"auto_save_minutes":5,"clip_keep_last":100,"theme":"dark","enable_auto_clip":false}'
    echo "$CONFIG_JSON" > "$CONFIG_FILE"
  fi
}

save_config() {
  echo "$CONFIG_JSON" > "$CONFIG_FILE"
  echo "[crecall] Config saved: $CONFIG_FILE"
}

set_config_field() {
  local field="$1" val="$2"
  CONFIG_JSON=$(python3 - "$field" "$val" <<'PY'
import sys, json
field, val = sys.argv[1:3]
cfg = json.loads(sys.stdin.read())
# type inference
if val.lower() in {"true","false"}:
    v = val.lower() == "true"
else:
    try:
        v = int(val)
    except ValueError:
        v = val
cfg[field] = v
print(json.dumps(cfg))
PY
)
}

settings_menu() {
  load_config
  echo "━━━━━━━━ SETTINGS ━━━━━━━━"
  echo "Current configuration:"
  echo "$CONFIG_JSON" | python3 -m json.tool 2>/dev/null || echo "$CONFIG_JSON"
  echo "Select option to modify:";
  echo " 1) Auto-save interval (minutes)"
  echo " 2) Clip retention (keep last N)"
  echo " 3) Theme (dark/light)"
  echo " 4) Enable auto-clip (true/false)"
  echo " 5) Cancel"
  read -r choice
  case "$choice" in
    1) echo "Enter minutes:"; read -r v; set_config_field auto_save_minutes "$v";;
    2) echo "Enter N:"; read -r v; set_config_field clip_keep_last "$v";;
    3) echo "Enter theme (dark/light):"; read -r v; set_config_field theme "$v";;
    4) echo "Enable auto-clip (true/false):"; read -r v; set_config_field enable_auto_clip "$v";;
    5) echo "Cancelled"; return 0;;
    *) echo "Invalid"; return 1;;
  esac
  save_config
}

main "$@"
